  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1028 PM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nUpper high stays broad over the desert southwest through Wednesday. \nTuesday is still looking like the hottest day for the area where \ntriple digits will be common across the desert lowlands. A Heat \nAdvisory is in effect for Tuesday afternoon for El Paso county and \nthe Lower Valley where high temperatures will be 105F+. The Lower\nValley may reach Heat Advisory criteria again on Thursday but \nlooks like El Paso will fall a couple degrees short of Advisory \ncriteria. Hot temperatures persist into the weekend but won't be \nquite as hot. Upper 90s and lower triple digits expected during \nthat time. Expect thunderstorm chances each day with a focus over \nthe Gila region and western NM locations bordering AZ being \nfavored. \n\nHeading into Thursday, upper high shifts to the Four Corners region \nand seems to stay put through the weekend. Could see a potential \nuptick in activity/coverage later in the work week, and maybe even \ninto the weekend, if we can get a little better tap of moisture from \nthe Gulf.",
